<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bandar Abbas</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bandar Abbas is a port on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persian-gulf">Persian Gulf</a> coast of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, named after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbas-i-of-persia">Shah Abbas I</a>, who developed it after capturing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hormuz">Hormuz</a> from the Portuguese in 1622. It became Iran's main port for trade with European companies. It was important for the trade and naval ambitions of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afsharid-empire">Afsharid Empire</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nader-shah">Nader Shah</a>.</p></div>
